{"parse":{"title":"2026–27 UEFA Nations League D","pageid":72856424,"revid":1379947554,"redirects":[],"wikitext":"{{Use dmy dates|date=February 2026}}\n{{Infobox international football competition\n| tourney_name   = UEFA Nations League D\n| year           = 2026–27\n| dates          = 24 September – 16 November 2026\n| num_teams      = 6\n| promoted       = {{fb|AND}}<br>{{fb|AZE}}<br>{{fb|GIB}}<br>{{fb|LIE}}<br>{{fb|LTU}}<br>{{fb|MLT}}\n| matches        = 8\n| goals          = 11\n| attendance     = {{#invoke:Football attendance summation|main|groups=leagued}}\n| top_scorer     = {{fbicon|MLT}} [[Teddy Teuma]]<br>(2 goals)\n| updated        = 4 October 2026\n| prevseason     = [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League D|2024–25]]\n}}\nThe '''2026–27 UEFA Nations League D''' is the fifth and final season of the fourth and lowest division of the [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League|2026–27 edition]] of the [[UEFA Nations League]], an international [[Association football|football]] competition involving the men's national teams of the member associations of [[UEFA]].\n\n==Format==\nLeague D consists of the six lowest-ranked UEFA members from 49–54 in the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League#Final overall ranking|2024–25 UEFA Nations League final overall ranking]], split into two groups of three. Each team will play four matches within their group, using the home-and-away [[round-robin tournament|round-robin]] on matchdays in September, October, and November 2026.<ref name=\"need to know\">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0298-1d6ef1acfaef-b54fcf1da859-1000/ |title=2026/27 UEFA Nations League: All you need to know |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=9 February 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref> Due to the removal of League D for the 2028–29 edition of the Nations League, all teams will be promoted to League C.<ref name=\"regulations\">{{cite web |url=https://documents.uefa.com/r/Regulations-of-the-UEFA-Nations-League-2026/27-Online |title=Regulations of the UEFA Nations League 2026/27 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=December 2025 |access-date=13 December 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260211170553/https://documents.uefa.com/api/khub/maps/HlG1NvOr4H_30IjSKzlRKg/attachments/2b1W4zSbckOh3ZMUhu0_wg-HlG1NvOr4H_30IjSKzlRKg/content |archive-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\nOriginally, the format for promotion and relegation would have involved only the group winners of League D being promoted, as well as the two worst last-placed teams in League C being relegated. The promotion/relegation play-offs would have concerned all runners-up in League C, with extra play-offs concerning the two best last-places in League C and both runners-up in League D to be held in March 2028. However, due to the [[UEFA Nations League#Post-2028 review and proposed format changes|changes scheduled for the 2028–29 UEFA Nations League]], in which the competition will be reduced from four leagues to three leagues of 18 teams, promotion/relegation was rebalanced to make all three upcoming leagues be at 18 teams.<ref>{{cite web |date=15 September 2026 |title=New promotion/relegation system for UEFA Nations League 2026/27 |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a9-21985b7e3370-3f0fda209606-1000/promotion_and_relegation_unl_website.pdf |access-date=18 September 2026 |publisher=[[UEFA]]}}</ref> This makes the 2026–27 UEFA Nations League the final edition to include League D.\n\n==Teams==\nLeague D includes six teams based on the results of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League|2024–25 season]]: the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League C#Ranking of fourth-placed teams|two worst-ranked group fourth-placed teams]] teams from [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League C#Groups|League C]], the two losers of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League promotion/relegation play-offs#League C vs League D|League C/D play-offs]] and the two third-placed teams from [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League D#Groups|League D]].\n\n===Team changes===\nThe following were the team changes in League D from the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League D|2024–25 season]]:<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0292-1c2abf3ccd56-d65f5c73f690-1000/ |title=Nations League final standings: Who made the quarter-finals? Who's been promoted? Who's been relegated? Who's in the play-offs? |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=22 November 2024 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0296-1d165d4a3647-4d55eede66c2-1000/ |title=Nations League play-offs: Results, promotion and relegation |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=23 March 2025 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n{|\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:200px\"\n|+ Incoming\n|-\n! Relegated from<br />[[2024–25 UEFA Nations League C|Nations League C]]\n|-\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|AZE}}\n* {{fb|LTU}}\n}}\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:200px\"\n|+ Outgoing\n|-\n! Promoted to<br />[[2026–27 UEFA Nations League C|Nations League C]]\n|-\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|MDA}}\n* {{fb|SMR}}\n}}\n|}\n|}\n\n===Seeding===\nTeams were seeded for the league phase based on the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League#Final overall ranking|2024–25 Nations League final overall ranking]], considering promotion and relegation between the leagues.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/029a-1df96111817a-2669251e926b-1000/unl_final_overall_rankings_after_unlf_2025.pdf |title=Final overall rankings of the UEFA Nations League 2024/25 (updated following the UNL finals 2025) |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=24 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a1-1fc00969b028-b36e773fcfc7-1000/20260123_circular_2026_03_en.zip |title=UEFA Nations League 2026/27 – League phase draw and fixture list procedures |number=03/2026 |magazine=UEFA Circular Letter |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=23 January 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n{|\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 1\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Team\n! {{Tooltip|Rank|Ranking (all UEFA teams)}}\n|-\n| {{fb|AZE}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 49\n|-\n| {{fb|LTU}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 50\n|-\n| {{fb|MLT}}{{refn|group=note|name=Identity|The identity of the two promotion/relegation play-off winners was not known at the time of the draw.}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 51\n|-\n| {{fb|GIB}}{{refn|group=note|name=Identity}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 52\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 2\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Team\n! {{Tooltip|Rank|Ranking (all UEFA teams)}}\n|-\n| {{fb|LIE}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 53\n|-\n| {{fb|AND}}\n| style=\"text-align:center\" | 54\n|}\n|}\n\nThe draw for the league phase took place in [[Brussels]], Belgium, on 12 February 2026, 18:00 [[Central European Time|CET]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/draws/2027/2002276/ |title=League phase draw |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/02a1-1fc60cd57c4d-de2c1d716ed6-1000/ |title=Draw for the league phase of the 2026/27 UEFA Nations League |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=11 February 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref> Groups were drawn to contain two teams from pot 1 and one team from pot 2.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a2-1fe81f47532b-33ea7fae9cab-1000/20260123_circular_2026_03_en_enclosure_1_unl_2627_league_phase_draw_procedure_en_1.pdf |title=League phase draw procedure |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=12 February 2026 |access-date=13 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n==Groups==\nThe fixture list was confirmed by UEFA on 13 February 2026, the day following the draw.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/02a2-1fea18abbcbc-456e846509e7-1000/ |title=2026/27 UEFA Nations League: All the league phase fixtures |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=13 February 2026 |access-date=13 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://editori